# {{.data_product_name}}

An MLOps project on Databricks, scaffolded from the LEGO MLOps template. It ships a working
example (an anime-score predictor over sandbox data in the `{{.data_product_name}}` catalog) so the
CI/CD wiring runs off the shelf — edit the example scripts to fit your own data product.

## Components included

This project was generated with:

- **Data preparation** — `src/{{.data_product_name}}/data_preprocessing.py`
- **Model training** — `src/{{.data_product_name}}/model/train_model.py`
- **Model evaluation + registry** — RMSE logging + champion-alias promotion (`src/common/mlflow_helper.py`)
- **Provenance tag** — `source_template=mlops_template` on every MLflow run, registered model and model version (`src/common/mlflow_helper.py`) and on every job in the bundle (`presets.tags` in `databricks.yml`). Find models with `mlflow.search_model_versions("tags.source_template = 'mlops_template'")`; jobs are filterable by tag in the Jobs UI and in `system.lakeflow` usage tables.
- **Continuous integration** — `tests/` + `.github/workflows/unit_test.yml`
- **Continuous delivery** — `databricks.yml` targets + `.github/`
{{- if eq .include_ray "yes" }}
- **Ray distributed training** — `src/{{.data_product_name}}/model/train_model_ray.py` (GPU job)
{{- end }}
{{- if eq .include_hyperparameter_tuning "yes" }}
- **Hyperparameter tuning** — `src/{{.data_product_name}}/model/tune_model_ray.py` (Ray Tune + Optuna)
{{- end }}
{{- if eq .include_serving "yes" }}
- **Model serving** — `src/{{.data_product_name}}/model/serve.py` (real-time endpoint)
{{- end }}
{{- if eq .include_batch_prediction "yes" }}
- **Batch prediction** — `src/{{.data_product_name}}/batch_prediction.py`
{{- end }}
{{- if eq .include_data_monitoring "yes" }}
- **Data monitoring** — `src/data_monitoring/data_drift_report.py` (Lakehouse quality monitor)
{{- end }}
{{- if and (eq .include_serving "yes") (eq .include_data_monitoring "yes") }}
- **Prediction drift monitoring** — `src/{{.data_product_name}}/monitoring/` (unpacks the serving
  endpoint's AI Gateway payload table, then attaches a Lakehouse `InferenceLog` monitor)
{{- end }}

## Adapt to your data product

The example carries anime-specific logic (target column `Score`, id `Name`, genre one-hot). Edit:

- `src/{{.data_product_name}}/data_preprocessing.py` — read your source table, build your features
- `src/{{.data_product_name}}/model/train_model.py` + `model/model_config.yml` — your model + params
- `databricks.yml` variables and `resources/{{.data_product_name}}/*.yml` job schedules/clusters

`catalog` (defaults to `{{.data_product_name}}`) and `schema` (`{{.schema}}`) are bundle variables
in `databricks.yml`. The raw source table defaults to the shared sandbox
`ai_enablement.general_resources.anime_bronze` so the example runs off the shelf — point
`{{.data_product_name}}_source_table` at your own data.

## Prerequisites

**Local**
- Python (see `pyproject.toml`) and [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)
- [Databricks CLI](https://docs.databricks.com/en/dev-tools/cli/index.html) configured with a profile

**CI/CD** — a registered data product with a NEXUS catalog, GitHub project, and dev/qa/prod
service principals set as environment secrets.

## Local development

```bash
uv sync --all-extras
uv run pytest -q
databricks bundle validate -t local --profile <your-profile>
```

## Deploy & run

```bash
databricks bundle deploy -t local --profile <your-profile>
databricks bundle run model_training_job -t local --profile <your-profile>
```

Deployment is symmetric across environments and tied to branches: `dev/**` → dev, pull requests
→ qa, `release/*` → prod (see `.github/`).

